I'd say "mi dunda lo plise ku do". "fa'a" is not a proper preposition but a=
=20
spatial tense marker (though all tense markers can be used as prepositions)=
=20
and doesn't denote motion unless preceded by "mo'i".

> zo'e pe do - =DE=D4=CF-=D4=CF =CF =D4=C5=C2=C5
"pe" isn't a preposition. It can be used to attach a prepositional phrase t=
o a=20
sumti (e.g. "le renro pe pa'o lo canko" means "the thrower who is through a=
=20
window", which is different from "le renro be pa'o lo canko" which means "t=
he=20
thrower through a window", i.e. he throws something through a window). "pe"=
 is=20
in the same selma'o as "goi", which does something quite un-preposition-lik=
e.

